title: 'parachains/disputes: remove the dead ValidatorSetCounts storage item'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    ## Summary

    Found while auditing for unused storage items (#13507). `ValidatorSetCounts` in the slashing pallet (`polkadot/runtime/parachains/src/disputes/slashing.rs`) is never read or written anywhere in the codebase. `ValidatorSetCount` (the value it would have cached) is always computed fresh from the session info or the key ownership proof where it's actually needed, instead of going through this storage map.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: patch
